# Woodland Acolyte // Mend the Wilds: "Put target permanent card from your graveyard on top of your library." Turn 3 Bot1
# Disenchants Bot2's Ornithopter: Bot2's graveyard now holds a permanent card, but not Bot1's, so Mend the Wilds cannot be
# cast on it; Bot1's own graveyard holds only Disenchant, an instant card, so there is no legal target at all. The Ornithopter
# stays in Bot2's graveyard and the Acolyte in Bot1's hand.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Disenchant
Woodland Acolyte
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Disenchant.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
! Bot1.Hand.Woodland Acolyte.Cast(Bot2.Graveyard.Ornithopter; Ability: Mend the Wilds)
! Bot1.Hand.Woodland Acolyte.Cast(Bot1.Graveyard.Disenchant; Ability: Mend the Wilds)

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot1.Hand = Island; Island; Island; Woodland Acolyte
